Bugfix: Do not resend files the server rejected in a bulk upload on every run

Small new files are uploaded together in one request. When the server rejected
single files of such a request, for example because the quota was exceeded, a
virus was found or permissions were missing, the client did not remember the
failure and sent the same files again with every sync run.

Rejected files now get an entry in the error list like files of a single
upload. The next attempt after the waiting time uploads the file on its own, so
the usual handling of the status code applies, including the quota hint and
growing waiting times.
